<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24403" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">interpŏsĭtĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		interpono, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a putting between</i>, <i>insertion.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tetrastyli, propter columnarum interpositiones,
					spatiosiores constituantur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					5, 3, 8</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Esp. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>An inserting</i> or <i>introduction</i> of persons in discourse: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">personarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Inv. 1, 6, 8</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">of words: una interpositio difficilior est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fam. 16, 22, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> A
			rhet. figure, <i>parenthesis</i>, <i><span class="en">Quint. 9,
				3, 23</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
